                <pb facs="0241" n="191" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg191"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/78a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-05-15T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 15, 1917, 4
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1404. The following Advisory Commission of Railway Experts to Russia has been
                    appointed: John F. Stevens, chairman;
                        John G. Greiner, George Gibbs,
                        W. L. Darling, Henry Miller,
                    members; accompanied by Franklin Reading, secretary and
                    disbursing officer; Edward P. Shannon, secretary;
                        C. A. Decker, stenographer; Eugene C.
                        Stevens, clerk; Leslie R. Fellows,
                    stenographer.</p>
                <p>They sailed on the 14th instant from Vancouver by the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Empress of India</hi> and will arrive at Vladivostok.</p>
                <p>Advise Government in order that proper instructions may be sent to Russian
                    authorities at Vladivostok.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
